     triggers.push_back(new TriggerNode("revive from corpse", { NextAction("revive from corpse", relevance) }));
-    triggers.push_back(new TriggerNode("master loot roll", { NextAction("master loot roll", relevance) }));
+    // local: the "master loot roll" TriggerNode was removed, not rewired. No trigger context
+    // registers that name, so it resolved to nullptr and was skipped on every tick; and
+    // MasterLootRollAction is strictly weaker than LootRollAction anyway - it votes on one
+    // roll with CalculateRollVote(proto) alone, skipping the armour-token, recipe and
+    // weapon/armour branches. Its packet (SMSG_LOOT_START_ROLL) now feeds "loot roll", which
+    // is registered and already has a node here. See PlayerbotAI's constructor.
 
